From 3f33cc441050cec88f24a69fce1de1846e901b83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anees Iqbal <hello@aneesiqbal.ai>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:26:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 50/68] draw+contract: a DontCare attachment keeps the contents
 it declared undefined
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Vulkan arm narrowed a three-valued MTLLoadAction to `load_seed: bool`
("LOAD vs CLEAR"), derived from whether a seed was resolved rather than from
the guest's ordinal. DontCare therefore reached `caches.rs` with the same key
as Clear and became `AttachmentLoadOp::CLEAR` against the record's clear
colour, so every texel a pass did not itself draw was overwritten.

Metal's DontCare declares the prior contents *undefined*, and undefined permits
any contents including the ones already there. Preserving is therefore a legal
realization of it and clearing is the only reading that destroys. The guest
relies on the preserving one: it declares DontCare and redraws only its damage
rect. `backend::metal::render` already hands the same wire word to Metal, which
preserves — so the two backends disagreed about one attachment prefix, and only
the Vulkan arm lost content.

Component: crates/reims-vgpu, x86 macOS / Linux Vulkan pathway (the Metal arm
was already correct and is unchanged).

Behavior. `LoadAction::preserves_prior_contents` is the single spelling of the
rule, a `match` so a fourth action fails the build there once rather than being
folded into a caller's catch-all. Three attachment rails ask it:

- colour slot 0 now enters the same seed doors as Load, so a DontCare that can
  be served its prior contents resolves a seed and the pass keys to LOAD. With
  nothing to serve it still clears, and `note_load_action_dont_care` now reports
  only that residual case rather than the whole population.
- secondary attachments have no seed door, so the key bit is gated on
  `resident_content_ready` for the attachment's identity. That gate is
  load-bearing rather than cautious: the target pool recycles an image across
  surfaces and inserts the recycled slot `content_ready=false`, so a LOAD taken
  without it would composite onto the previous tenant's pixels. Load's own
  behavior is unchanged; only DontCare is widened.
- depth asks the same, and needed no new gate — `honours_load` already degrades
  an unanswerable load to CLEAR by name.

The two preserving actions differ only in where they land when nothing can
answer, and they differ because the contract's strictness differs: a Load
requires the prior contents (and `load_seed_lost` names the shortfall), while a
DontCare merely permits them.

Measurement. On a driven macos-15 boot the defect showed as `passbegin_clear`
running *exactly* `color0_declared_dontcare` above the clears the guest asked
for — 67, 70, 247, 704 and 280 on five boots, an identity rather than a
correlation, which also proves every DontCare pass took the clear arm. After
the change that excess is 30 against 48 declared, and the full-screen 1920x1080
DontCare clear every prior boot carried is gone. Area was ~18M attachment
pixels a boot, near-constant across boots.

Tests. `only_a_clear_refuses_the_attachments_prior_contents` pins the predicate
(including that an out-of-contract ordinal folds to DontCare and so preserves);
`a_dontcare_colour_attachment_is_still_served_its_prior_contents` is the
behavioural half over `type11_load_is_a_seed_candidate`. Full suite green
(2222 lib + 7 integration binaries); clippy -D warnings clean on all three arms
(native vulkan, aarch64-apple-darwin backend-metal, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu).

Not verified. This does NOT fix the intermittent white-desktop / missing-Dock
defect on macos-15 — a driven boot carrying this change still reproduced the
white background, so that class is eliminated as its cause and remains open.
No Apple-host arm was run, so the Metal backend is compile-only here. Secondary
and depth coverage is unmeasured: MRT and stencil traffic is near zero on this
workload, so only slot 0's repair has a boot reading behind it.

